  "scope": "Windows/Linux each pass 22 native suites, three existing full C++ workflow/batch/RGB UI regression probes, one installed public C++ SDK consumer exercising RGB workflow publication, ten background repetitions, four hidden GL contexts and 5438 installed Python checks, zero failure/error/skip. There are 664 new cases: 546 saved/authored program executions of 273 actual ImageJ 1.54r RGB Apply reference rows; 72 native uniform target/ROI/component/history combinations; 11 authored grammar, seven complete-original/target/budget, four disabled-intent, two mixed/evolving-stage, one late stage-type refusal, four cancellation/failure/stale, 12 portable session Batch, three Batch cleanup and two per-input Batch setup transport cases. Whole-program metadata descriptors throw on plane access; native RGB reset metadata feeds later conversions without samples. Actual execution uses preceding-stage pixels, with empty-mask no-change behavior and paired final history. Native fixtures additionally validate public C++ program serialization/publication, session Batch input preservation and real mouse/key/text Run parameter editing with invalid then corrected component input, explicit confirmation, Prepare, Apply and Undo/Redo. Saved captures remain immutable when authored options override them. RGB and scalar public Apply headers/wire profiles and portable program schemas remain unchanged; one operation token is added. Actual compiled native inputs and installed module origins are pinned. Linux uses a SHA-verified native snapshot of 5469 test/config/fixture files. Two test-only amendments after native qualification remove accidental patch markers and fix test access to immutable Python intent; before/after identities and original variants are retained. Owned prototype/final scratch is CRC/member-SHA archived before deletion; final qualified installs, consumer/probes, logs and reports remain. Original 99 requirement/status triples, existing input registrations and commercial-use dependency inventory are preserved. RGB histogram/Auto, exact ImageJ stack/controller/slider semantics and full G057/ImageJ/Fiji/platform/resource acceptance remain open. The workflow uses the documented native uniform multi-axis mapping and paired Undo extension.",
